"answer": "Project Zenith is an AI-driven initiative launched in 2029 aimed at developing advanced mental health support systems to enhance accessibility and reduce stigma. The project utilizes AI chatbots, virtual therapists, and community forums, with a goal to reach 5 million users by 2035. Key updates include the approval of a $2M budget (with specific allocations of $550,000 for general scope and $55,000 for compliance), team expansions adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, and a move into the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The project is also gathering R&D ideas for data visualization tools, exploring partnerships with TechInnovate, and updating security protocols to include multi-factor authentication and encryption."
